  "counterexample": {
    "setup": "200 valid authoritative MV shards including a matching upstream source, then an unrelated shard with CURRENT naming a missing manifest",
    "baseline": "MvCatalog.list throws RocksDBException; the existing allMvsCached catch converts the entire catalog read to an empty sequence",
    "point_candidate": "Verified source point lookup succeeds and never observes the unrelated shard failure, even with missing/legacy/error fallback",
    "consequence": "Same fresh source schema and persisted upstream identity produce different fingerprints: baseline schema_drift, prototype pass.",
    "decision": "Do not replace schema resolution with this point prototype. Checking only successful candidate names cannot preserve whole-read failure semantics. This is a counterexample to the tested candidate, not a proof that every possible catalog optimization is impossible."
  },
  "alias_and_mutation_findings": [
    "Schema identity matching is exact metadata db.table first, then an unqualified metadata key. It is not a consumer reverse-dependency lookup.",
    "An unrelated namespace may intentionally fall back to a db-less MV with the same short name; exact namespace matches override that fallback.",
    "A real registered Delta operational alias shares a physical location and schema with its source but contributes no MV identity when its lexical key is absent.",
    "Legacy missing definition identities use full enumeration and legacy hashing.",
    "Create/drop/recreate and definition-property changes are re-read; in-flight source-version advancements still reject dependent schema resolution.",
    "A simultaneous upsert writer and point readers observed current generations; a completed generation was always visible without a success cache.",
    "Fresh local state restored from a real file-backed state-sync publication retained the same lookup and full-read identities.",
    "OpenIvmStateBarrier.withMutation takes a read lock and is gated by state sync. It is not a writer-excluding catalog epoch; sharing snapshots across concurrent commands would require additional independently proven mutation semantics.",
    "The original allMvsCached value is reused by downstream/cascade decisions. Moving a schema scan can merely move the same enumeration downstream, so no whole-refresh improvement is inferred from this diagnostic."
  ],
  "no_win_policy": "No production switch or cache was introduced. Base-table/no-match paths retain a full enumeration and add validation work in the prototype; the prototype remains unadopted on every path.",
